## Issue 1 — ai_service: attach a per-alert embedding to every ProcessedAlert

**Labels:** `area:ai-service` · `type:feature` · `plan:1`

**Context**
The incident-clustering engine needs a per-alert semantic vector to group
*unrecognized* failures (the novel path). Recognized failures don't use it, but
every alert must carry one so clustering keeps working even when the LLM breaker
is open. Reuse the sentence-transformers encoder already loaded by
`ai_service/semcache.py` — no second model.

**Scope** (plan Tasks 1–3)
- Add `embedding: list[float] | None` to `ProcessedAlert` (`shared/models.py`).
- Add `SemanticCache.embed(message) -> list[float] | None` reusing the loaded
  encoder + `normalize()` (`ai_service/semcache.py`). Note: this is a real
  `encode()` call per alert — the cache's fast exact-match path does **not**
  already produce a vector.
- Attach the embedding to every emitted `ProcessedAlert` on **all** paths —
  cache-hit, AI, and fallback (`ai_service/graph.py`), off the fetch path.

**Acceptance criteria**
- [ ] `ProcessedAlert` round-trips `embedding` over the `processed.alerts` queue.
- [ ] Every non-suppressed WARN/ERROR alert carries an embedding, including
      `source="fallback"` (LLM down).
- [ ] Embedding is computed from the **normalized** message (masked ids/numbers),
      same `normalize()` the cache uses.
- [ ] No second model instance is loaded; unit tests for `embed()` and
      attachment (`tests/test_models.py`, `tests/test_semcache.py`).

**Out of scope:** anything in the backend; storage of the vector.

